    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field following the existing `displayName` pattern exactly, keeping structural impact minimal by touching only two files and adding no new complexity to any method:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (right beside the existing `displayName`), which regenerates the `OwnerDto` with the new field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` annotation to the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\",\n       expression = \"java((owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1) + \\\".\\\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1) + \\\".\\\").toUpperCase())\")\n   ```\n\nFor `firstName=\"john\"`, `lastName=\"smith\"` this yields `\"J.S.\"`. `firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty`, so `substring(0,1)` is always safe. No method bodies grew and no cyclomatic complexity was added \u2014 the change is a declarative annotation plus a schema property.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` and the full suite are green.",
